Add the DADAO exception model (DG-004c), spec-derived (§2.5/§2.6/§3.1/§3.7,
ADR-0004), never from QEMU cpu.c/translate.c. SE exit codes shared with the
harness FAULT_CODES: ILLI=0x82, MALIGN=0x81, UNDI=0x83.

faults.{hh,cc}: DADAOFault now carries (name, exit code); invoke() exits the
sim loop with it. Add IlliFault(0x82)/MalignFault(0x81)/UndiFault(0x83) and a
private UnimplFault(0x7F) sentinel (unimplemented opcode → adapter SKIP).

decoder.cc legality (return the fault before any register/memory write, per
the §2.7 precise-exception rule):
  - ILLI: rdha/rdhb-destination = rd0 (RR2R/RI2R families, load/store/multi,
    addi-rd/rb); rbha/rbhb = rb0 (RB load/store, addi-rb); dual-dest both rd0
    or same reg (add/sub/muls/mulu/divs/divu); div-by-zero and INT64_MIN÷-1;
    multi immu6=0 and first+immu6>64; register block-copy legality; unimp.
  - MALIGN: single & multi load/store whose EA is not width-aligned (§3.1).
  - UNDI: reserved encodings (unallocated major op, reserved MISC-Norm minor)
    via UnknownInst. Distinct from ILLI — reserved ≠ illegal-operand (QEMU once
    conflated these in DL-043b; gem5 splits them from the spec).

Reserved vs unimplemented: control flow beyond jump-iiii (br*, jump_r, call,
ret) and register-bank block-copy *semantics* are defined-but-unimplemented →
AbstainInst/BlockCopyStub raise UnimplFault (SKIP), NOT UNDI. Block-copy still
enforces its ILLI legality.

Spot-checked distinct codes: ILLI=130, MALIGN=129, UNDI=131 (reserved major op
and reserved MISC-Norm minor), halt=0.

3-way differential: AGREE(3-way) 131 -> 162, DIVERGE=0. Every expected_fault
vector now PASSes (FAIL=0). Remaining 36 gem5-SKIP are control-flow branch and
register block-copy *semantics* (functional, not faults — future work). Smokes
42/42/0.

